27 coins, 15-minute bars, five years.

Side selection is the ONLY thing that changes between rows.

  variant                         episodes     per ep       t   win    worst   CAGR 1x    maxDD  Sharpe
  both sides always (registered)    82,366   +0.1157%  +17.60   49%   -24.3%     60.1%    -5.3%    4.12
  biased: long up / short down      40,272   -0.0357%   -5.08   35%   -20.2%     -7.1%   -31.1%   -1.23
  contrarian: long down / short up    71,751   -0.0148%   -2.39   52%   -24.3%     -5.7%   -28.4%   -0.50
  long side only                    41,532   +0.0941%  +10.20   49%   -23.0%     20.9%    -9.1%    1.74
  short side only                   40,834   +0.1377%  +14.70   49%   -24.3%     32.0%    -6.8%    2.89

  If 'biased' wins, DK's directional overlay is right and the book
  should stop fighting the coin's own trend. If 'contrarian' wins,
  the intuition is backwards and the book earns precisely by taking
  the side the trend argues against — which is what mean reversion is.
